{
  // ⛔⛔ THE STAGING SITE HOST FOR EVERY TOWN. One Worker, one route, forever.
  //
  // WHY THIS EXISTS AND WHY IT IS NOT CLOUDFLARE PAGES (ruled 2026-09-21):
  // the address is `staging.theward.online/<map>/`, one per Map, and publishing one town
  // must not touch another. Pages deploys a whole site atomically, so N towns in one
  // project means every press rebuilds and reships every town — which is exactly the
  // "one trunk, one deploy" defect the ruling settled against — and one project per town
  // serves a HOSTNAME, not a subpath, so it cannot produce the ruled address at all.
  //
  // ⭐ THE SHAPE IS THE SLAB LAYER'S, DELIBERATELY. `bakedUrl.js`: "one prefix per look
  // under one bucket, so pouring town #2 needs no code change and no entry in any table."
  // A town's SITE is now a second prefix under the same roof, written by the same pour.
  // A new town needs no project, no key, no DNS record and no edit here.
  "$schema": "../../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "theward-staging-sites",
  "main": "src/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-01",
  "observability": { "enabled": true },
  // ⭐ The one address, bound from here rather than by hand. ⚠️ The dashboard's "Connect
  // domain" dialog answered "No zones match staging.theward.online" for this same zone —
  // it was wrong, and `wrangler deploy` created the custom domain without complaint
  // (2026-09-21). ⛔ Don't re-diagnose the zone on the dashboard's word; the CLI is the
  // authority. ▶ npx wrangler r2 bucket domain list theward-assets  (zone_name: theward.online)
  "routes": [{ "pattern": "staging.theward.online", "custom_domain": true }],
  // ⛔ NO `*.workers.dev` ADDRESS. It was disabled as a side effect of adding the route
  // above; it is declared here so it stays off ON PURPOSE. A second ungated public URL
  // serving the same towns is exactly the bulk-access surface `SECURITY.md` F-18 is about,
  // and an unlisted partner link is worth nothing if the same bytes sit at a second address
  // nobody is watching. ⚠️ It also means there is no fallback URL while DNS settles — that
  // is accepted, not overlooked.
  "workers_dev": false,
  "preview_urls": false,
  "r2_buckets": [
    // The same bucket the slab already lives in. Sites go under `staging/sites/<map>/`,
    // slabs under `staging/baked/<look>/` — two prefixes, one roof.
    { "binding": "ASSETS", "bucket_name": "theward-assets" }
  ],
  "vars": {
    "SITE_PREFIX": "staging/sites/",
    // The ONE player build every town is served from.
    "PLAYER_PREFIX": "staging/player/"
  }
}
